<p class="eyebrow">Configuration</p>

{{#if isConfigured}}
  <h1>Azure AD B2C is configured</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The app read a complete configuration from the environment and is running as
    a <strong>{{mode}}</strong> client.
  </p>
  <p class="alert alert--ok">Nothing to do here — head back and sign in.</p>
{{else}}
  <h1>Finish the Azure AD B2C setup</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Copy <code>.env.example</code> to <code>.env</code>, fill in the values from
    your B2C tenant, then restart the app.
  </p>

  <p class="alert alert--warn">
    Still missing:
    {{#each missing}}<code>{{this}}</code>{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}
  </p>
{{/if}}

<h2 class="section">In the Azure portal</h2>
<ol class="steps">
  <li>
    Create a sign-up/sign-in <strong>user flow</strong> (e.g.
    <code>B2C_1_signupsignin</code>) and put its name in
    <code>B2C_POLICY_NAME</code>. Under <em>Application claims</em>, tick
    <em>Email Addresses</em>, <em>Display Name</em>, <em>Given Name</em>,
    <em>Surname</em>, <em>Identity Provider</em> and <em>User's Object ID</em> —
    the welcome page reads exactly those claims.
  </li>
  <li>
    Take the tenant name from <em>Azure AD B2C &rarr; Overview &rarr; Domain
    name</em> (the part before <code>.onmicrosoft.com</code>) into
    <code>B2C_TENANT_NAME</code>.
  </li>
  <li>
    Register an app and copy its <em>Application (client) ID</em> into
    <code>B2C_CLIENT_ID</code>.
  </li>
  <li>
    Under <em>Authentication</em>, add <code>{{redirectUri}}</code> as a redirect
    URI on the <strong>Web</strong> platform. Registering it under
    <em>Mobile and desktop applications</em> — or setting <em>Allow public client
    flows</em> to <em>Yes</em> — makes B2C treat the app as a public client, which
    then rejects a client secret with <code>AADB2C90084</code>.
  </li>
  <li>
    Create a <strong>client secret</strong> under <em>Certificates &amp;
    secrets</em> and copy the <em>Value</em> (shown only once, and not the
    <em>Secret ID</em>) into <code>B2C_CLIENT_SECRET</code>.
    <strong>Optional:</strong> leave it empty to run as a public client, where the
    authorization code is redeemed with PKCE alone.
  </li>
  <li>
    Add <code>{{postLogoutRedirectUri}}</code> as a
    <strong>post logout redirect URI</strong> so sign-out returns here.
  </li>
</ol>

<p class="note">
  No implicit-grant settings are needed — this app uses the authorization code
  flow, so leave <em>Access tokens</em> and <em>ID tokens</em> unticked.
</p>

{{#if discoveryUrl}}
  <details class="claims">
    <summary>Discovery document the app will read at startup</summary>
    <pre>{{discoveryUrl}}</pre>
  </details>
{{/if}}

<div class="actions">
  <a class="button button--ghost" href="/">Back to home</a>
</div>
